cellGcmSys: run NV0039 buffer copies; keep 2D-engine state out of the draw engine's NV4097 registers.

NV0039 (libgcm's memory-to-memory copy, cellGcmSetTransferData) was not implemented: on subchannel 1 it was taken for
NV4097 state, and with GCM_SUBCH1_2D=1 it reached the 2D path, which only logged it. Resistance 3 streams its level
textures with it, from IO-mapped main memory into local memory, so every texture lost the part the copy carried (its
mip tail) and rendered as noise. BUFFER_NOTIFY now copies LINE_COUNT lines of LINE_LENGTH bytes between the DMA
contexts (local frame buffer or IO-mapped host memory), as RPCS3's nv0039::buffer_notify.

The register-file draw engine strips the subchannel, so it also took every 2D-engine method as NV4097 state (NV0039's
OFFSET_OUT is BLEND_ENABLE's number). It now gets only what the 3D path takes, plus the driver methods.

The copy's span (PITCH * (LINE_COUNT - 1) + LINE_LENGTH) and the end of the DMA range are computed in 64 bits: in 32
bits a derailed FIFO's pitch and line count wrapped them to a few bytes, the range passed the bounds check and the copy
then ran the real offsets gigabytes past the guest window into host memory. Such a copy is now dropped like one from an
unmapped context, and so is a range past the guest memory the host backs.

tests/gcm_nv0039 (ctest gcm_nv0039) runs a packed and a pitched copy through the FIFO walker, and four that must be
dropped (a strided and a packed span wrapping 32 bits, a range wrapping the IO space, local memory past the guest
window), each in a child process: without these checks all four run and die on SIGSEGV/SIGBUS.

Upstream: not proposed yet.

---

